        "original_id": "5071387e-1785-5c6e-947d-44a7a4d8bcd5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Teams: Miami Dolphins, Minnesota Vikings, New England Patriots, Tampa Bay\n- People: Mark Henderson, John Smith\n- Events: 1982 Miami Dolphins season, Snowplow Game\n- Places: snowy field, stadium\n\nFacts:\n- During the 1982 Miami Dolphins season, the Miami Dolphins lost to Tampa Bay and then defeated the Minnesota Vikings 22-14.\n- The next week in the 1982 Miami Dolphins season, the Miami Dolphins lost 3-0 to the New England Patriots in the game known as the Snowplow Game.\n- In the Snowplow Game, stadium snowplow operator Mark Henderson cleared a spot on the snowy field for New England Patriots kicker John Smith.\n- In the Snowplow Game, John Smith kicked the game-winning field goal to give the New England Patriots a 3-0 win over the Miami Dolphins.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
